                <h2>2026</h2>
            



		

		



		
				
			
	
    




        




    
    



    


<ul><li data-list-item-id="e04ecbc2923bdf5d2a447e1e4a764f087"><p style="margin-left:0px;">Johannes Tischer, Stephan Anzengruber, Martin Mienkina, Tim Dorittke, Julia Binder, Gregor Kasprian, Georg Langs and Roxane Licandro; <strong>ALRAU: Atlas Learning from Routine Antenatal Ultrasound; </strong>MICCAI 2026</p></li><li data-list-item-id="e5cccb4eb1fafc562e59f7b68dd7982e1"><p style="margin-left:0px;">Paulina Gebhart, Florian Heinzl, Chiara Kahl, Alev Bari, Georg Langs, Daniela Muhr, Christian F Singer, Yen Y Tan; <strong>Pathologic complete response and survival according to germline BRCA1/2 status in triple-negative breast cancer; </strong>Breast Cancer.; 2026 Sep 10; <a href="https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12282-026-01914-8" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">doi: 10.1007/s12282-026-01914-8</a> online ahead of Print.</p></li><li data-list-item-id="eed337b574dd5a8183066aecc9c00311c"><p style="margin-left:0px;">Daniela Prinz, Christoph Fürböck, Silvester J. Bartsch, Joachim Friske, Daniela Laimer-Gruber, Lena Zachhuber, Claudia Kuntner, Thomas Wanek, Georg Langs, Thomas H. Helbich &amp; Katja Pinker; <strong>A simple MRI-derived correction substantially reduces bias in caliper-based tumor volume estimation in subcutaneous tumor models ; </strong>Scientific reports. 2026 Sep 7</p></li><li data-list-item-id="e4b4839fec71164d37e0d8c5e90d6b564"><p style="margin-left:0px;">P. Kienast, M. Stuempflen, S. Glatter, G. Langs, D. Prayer, G. Kasprian; OP10.01: <strong>Altered developmental trajectory of the fetal cerebellar vermis in prenatal alcohol exposure: fetal MRI study; </strong>Ultrasound in Obstetrics and Gynecology; 2026 Aug 31; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/uog.70305_178" target="_blank" class="epub-doi" rel="noreferrer">https://doi.org/10.1002/uog.70305_178Digital Object Identifier (DOI)</a></p></li><li data-list-item-id="ea42250c3697bdc43daade835b209f4e5"><p style="margin-left:0px;">Ba-Ssalamah SA, Poetter-Lang S, Yitik AY, El-Aal TA, Ba-Ssalamah A, Ka